\@writefile{tdo}{\contentsline {todo}{We use the \emph  {biblatex} package to handle our references. We use the command \texttt  {parencite} to get a reference in parentheses or square brackets, like this \textbackslash parencite\{hioannidis\_coherent\_1991\}, resulting in \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\parencite {ioannidis_coherent_1991}. It is also possible to include the author as part of the sentence using \texttt  {textcite}, when talking about the work of \textbackslash textcite\{maguire\_jr\_new\_2014\} resulting in \blx@tocontentsinit {0}\textcite {maguire_jr_new_2014}.\\ This also means that you have to change the include files to include biblatex and change the way that the \texttt  {reference.bib} file is included.}{1}{section*.48}\protected@file@percent }
